---
import { createElement } from "react";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { routeForDoc } from "../lib/routes.mjs";
import { SITE } from "../site.config";
import { Button, Callout, Claim, EnforcementTag, Measurement, SourceMark, TitleBlock } from "../design-system/components/index.js";
import { RULES } from "../plugins/rehype-rungs.mjs";

// The mapping table is read from the plugin itself, so the page cannot advertise a rule the
// build does not run. A hand-kept copy of this table would be the exact failure the site argues
// against — the difference between a rule and a rule that is checked.
const done = RULES.filter((r) => r.status === "done");
const todo = RULES.filter((r) => r.status !== "done");

// The rule this page argues from is now on the wiki, so cite it there rather than off-site.
// createElement, not JSX: an .astro frontmatter block is TypeScript.
const governedBy = createElement("a", { href: routeForDoc("CLAUDE.md") }, "CLAUDE.md — the evidence rule");
---

<Base title="Contribute — rungs" width={1000}>
  <div class="sheet">
    <TitleBlock
      kicker="Contribute"
      title="Author a module"
      fields={[
        { label: "Governed by", value: governedBy },
        { label: "Updated", value: SITE.asOf },
      ]}
    />

    <section class="intro">
      <p class="lede">
        Everything here was paid for once already. A contribution is admitted when it carries its
        receipts: <Claim kind="evidence" cite="CLAUDE.md">
          every claim is evidenced — a file path, a commit, a measured count, or a quoted rule — or
          it is visibly marked as opinion.
        </Claim>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="sec">
      <span class="lab">Admission checks · all must hold</span>
      <div class="checks">
        <div class="check">
          <div class="check-t">1 · A module is a unit</div>
          <div class="check-b">
            It can be installed, checked, and removed as a unit. It owns files, and it owns the
            rules about those files.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="check">
          <div class="check-t">2 · Rules ship their checker</div>
          <div class="check-b">
            Every generated rule is tagged <EnforcementTag state="gated" /> or
            <EnforcementTag state="review-only" /> — no silent third category.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="check">
          <div class="check-t">3 · Procedures ship their entry point</div>
          <div class="check-b">
            A workflow with no invocation surface does not run. The skill lands in the same change
            as the doc.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="check">
          <div class="check-t">4 · Patterns name their sources</div>
          <div class="check-b">
            "Four repos converge" is checkable only if each pattern says which:
            <SourceMark sources={["HG", "HT"]} /> — or states its counter-example.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="check">
          <div class="check-t">5 · Costs are stated</div>
          <div class="check-b">
            Every practice names what it costs to run. A pattern without its cost gets recommended
            to repos that cannot afford it.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="check">
          <div class="check-t">6 · Counts carry receipts</div>
          <div class="check-b">
            <Measurement
              value="84 names checked; 56 taken, 28 free"
              date="2026-08-14"
              command="npm view <name> version"
            /> — count, date, command, one line.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sec">
      <span class="lab">Markdown → component mapping · the wiki renders plain markdown</span>
      <p class="body">
        Write plain markdown. Every rule below detects a convention the corpus already uses; none
        of them need an author-side wrapper. The table is read from
        <code>src/plugins/rehype-rungs.mjs</code> at build time.
      </p>
      <table class="map">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>rule</th><th>detected by</th><th>state</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            done.map((r) => (
              <tr>
                <td class="map-id">{r.id}</td>
                <td class="map-d">{r.detects}</td>
                <td><EnforcementTag state="gated" /></td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
          {
            todo.map((r) => (
              <tr class="is-todo">
                <td class="map-id">{r.id}</td>
                <td class="map-d">{r.detects}</td>
                <td><span class="rgs-enf rgs-enf-undeclared">not implemented</span></td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="mt">
        <Callout kind="gap" refId="mapping">
          Two things cannot be inferred from markdown: whether an unmarked prose sentence is
          evidenced (only measurements are mechanically detectable), and the capture date of a
          console fence. Both render their loud states rather than a confident default —
          {done.length} of {RULES.length} rules run today.
        </Callout>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sec actions">
      <Button href={`${SITE.repo}/blob/main/docs/decisions/ADR-0003-module-definition-format.md`}>
        Read the module format (ADR-0003)
      </Button>
      <Button variant="secondary" href={`${SITE.repo}/issues/new`}>Submit a pattern</Button>
      <span class="note">
        Abandoned practices are findings, not omissions — record retirements with their reason.
      </span>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .sheet {
    padding: 40px 0 64px;
  }
  .intro {
    padding: 32px 0 4px;
  }
  .lede {
    font: 400 16.5px/1.6 var(--font-serif);
    max-width: 68ch;
  }
  .sec {
    padding: 36px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .lab {
    font: 600 10px var(--font-label);
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .body {
    font: 400 14.5px/1.6 var(--font-serif);
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    max-width: 72ch;
  }
  .checks {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .check {
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--surface-card);
    padding: 12px 14px;
  }
  .check-t {
    font: 600 13px var(--font-display);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .check-b {
    font: 400 13.5px/1.6 var(--font-serif);
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .map {
    background: var(--surface-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .map-id {
    font: 500 12.5px var(--font-mono);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .map-d {
    font: 400 13px/1.5 var(--font-serif);
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .is-todo .map-id,
  .is-todo .map-d {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .mt {
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
  .actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .note {
    font: italic 400 13px var(--font-serif);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .checks {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
